# Virgil — Operational Memory

> **Setup**: copy this file to `config/memory.md` and customize for your own labels and routing rules.
> ```bash
> cp config/memory.md.example config/memory.md
> ```

Cross-session context. Read at session start, updated at session close.

---

## Labelling System

Notes from `Scratch_Pad/` are parsed, segmented (a single file may contain multiple items), and labelled during `/start`. Labelled notes are filed to `Archive/` as individual `.md` files. Tasks are routed to your task manager (see `config/user.md`).

### Default labels (customize for your life)

- **Lists** — reference lists that grow over time (e.g., books to read, restaurants to try). Kept as living documents.
- **Tasks** — action items and to-dos. Route to your task manager with Status: Inbox, Source: Virgil, Area if detectable.
- **Completed Tasks** — items you've done. Mark as Done in your task manager and record as daily wins in the daily note.
- **Goals** — weekly/monthly goals. Route to your Goals DB. Store in memory.md for reference.
- **Writings/Thoughts** — personal reflections, ideas, observations. Processed through the **Knowledge Distillation Pipeline** (see below).
- **Personal Development** — structured self-work: identity exercises, vision-building, growth frameworks.
- **Groceries** — food/household items to buy → append to `Archive/Shopping list.md`.
- **Kids — [Name]** — observations, quotes, milestones about a child → append to `Archive/[Name].md` with date and place.
- **[Your area]** — add labels for your own domains (e.g., "Business - X", "Side project Y", "Hobbies").

---

## Task Routing — Task Manager Integration

**Source of truth for tasks: the task manager configured in `config/user.md`.**

### How Virgil creates tasks

Minimum fields:
- **Name**: task title
- **Status**: always `Inbox` (your triage process picks them up from here)
- **Source**: always `Virgil`
- **Area**: set if detectable from context (see Area Detection Rules in `user.md`)

Optional metadata (e.g., Importance, Sprint, Project) is not Virgil's job — leave those for your triage process.

### Archive Linking (prevent orphan notes)

When creating a task, **always search the Archive for related notes** before submitting:
1. Use keywords from the task title, detected Area, and contextual terms to search `Archive/`.
2. If related notes found, add to task description as "Related vault notes: [names]".
3. Bidirectional: if filing a new Archive note that relates to an existing task, mention it in `## Related`.
4. Don't force it — only link genuinely related notes.

### Virgil CAN update task status

When user says "done with X" or "finished Y" during listening mode:
- Find the task in the task manager and mark Status → `Done`
- Log as a daily win in the daily note

### Daily Recap → Agent Updates

After writing the daily note during `/wrap-up`, post a copy to the Agent Updates DB (configured in `user.md`) with:
- **Title**: Short summary line
- **Source**: `Virgil`
- **Target**: `[Your triage agent or you]`
- **Type**: `Daily Recap`
- **Date**: Today's date
- **Page content**: The full daily recap text

### Fallback Queue

If the task manager API fails, write to `_notion_queue.md` at vault root.
Format: `- [Area] Task name | Status: Inbox | Source: Virgil`
On next `/start`, attempt to flush queued items. Remove successfully synced items.

### Duplicate Detection

Before creating a task, search the task manager for similar titles.
- In **listening mode**: flag briefly ("This looks similar to 'X' — create anyway?")
- In **/start processing**: include duplicates in confirmation summary

---

## Knowledge Distillation Pipeline

**Applies ONLY to: Writings/Thoughts label.** All other labels are unaffected. This pipeline is optional — remove this section if you don't want it.

### Architecture
- **Raw layer**: Ideas database (see `user.md` for ID). Store raw note unchanged with metadata.
- **Knowledge graph layer**: a separate vault (e.g., Obsidian) for conceptual knowledge graphs — path configurable.

### Node types
- **C - Title** (`#wt/concept`) — atomic ideas, hypotheses, models, insights.
- **L - Title** (`#wt/lens`) — interpretation frameworks. Create only when used repeatedly.
- **H - Title** (`#wt/hub`) — curated maps of related concept clusters. Create conservatively.

### Processing workflow
1. Store raw note in Ideas DB (Status: Not started → Done after processing)
2. Extract 2–3 atomic concepts (max 5). Prefer fewer strong ideas over many weak fragments.
3. Create concept notes using the template below
4. Link concepts to each other
5. Assign 0–2 lens nodes per concept
6. Add development questions, research directions, optional writing seeds

### Concept note template
```
# C - Title
Concept: [clear statement]
Explanation: [short expansion]
Status: seed | developing | structured | publishable
Source: [Raw Note title]

Related Concepts:
[[C - X]] — [relation explanation]

Lens:
[[L - X]]

## Development Questions
- ...

## Research Directions
- ...

## Writing Seed (optional)
```

### Quality rules
- No trivial fragments, no excessive splitting, no keyword-based linking
- Concept notes must be concise, conceptual, self-contained
- Duplicate detection: check existing concepts before creating

---

## Interlinking

All vault notes should be connected using `[[wikilinks]]`:
- **Atomic notes** — each file represents one concept, idea, or task.
- **Link on creation** — when filing a new note, link it to related existing notes.
- **Backlink both ways** — if note A links to note B, also add a link from B back to A.
- **Related section** — use `## Related` at the bottom of notes for thematic connections.
- **Daily notes link to everything** — daily notes link to all archived notes and tasks they reference.
- Don't force links. Only link when there's genuine conceptual connection.

---

## Daily Note — Two-Phase Design

### Phase 1 — Live capture (during the day)
- During listening mode, **every item is immediately appended** to the daily note as a raw bullet.
- Format: `- [HH:MM] Item description → routing`
- Purpose: **persistence** — if the session dies, nothing is lost.

### Phase 2 — Curated narrative (during /wrap-up)
- During `/wrap-up`, the raw capture log is refined into a curated editorial narrative.
- Lead with **Daily Wins**.
- Style: themes, areas of focus, tasks moved, editorial take on direction and momentum.

### Session recovery
- If interrupted, you can resume listening mode without re-running `/start`.
- Read the daily note to restore context.

---

## Session Log

_Operational session history. Append new entries at the bottom as you use Virgil._

(Empty on first install. Virgil will append session summaries here over time.)
